+
+### F-309 - Dot and rect paint could not vary per row
+
+- Status: resolved
+- Severity: medium
+- Owner: API
+- Observed in: Solenoid's Recharts-to-TanStack migration
+  (`src/graph/components/chartRender.tsx` and
+  `src/graph/components/charts/heatFigures.tsx`)
+- Friction: XY points coloured through a numeric colormap and heatmap cells
+  whose rows already carried their paint needed per-row fills. `dot` and `rect`
+  accepted only a constant `fill` and `stroke`, while bar, area, text, line,
+  and link accept a visual channel. The application routed each prepared CSS
+  color through `color` and a pass-through color resolver whose mapping
+  returned its input, so the color scale did no work.
+- Decision: make `fill` and `stroke` visual channels on `dot`, `rect`, and
+  `cell`. A resolved `fill` replaces the color scale for that row and becomes
+  its interaction color, as it does for bars.
+- Verification: point-color tests resolve per-row fills, strokes, and point
+  colors for `dot` and `cell`, and fail against the constant-only marks.
